        "id": "p31-q11-a",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "a",
        "prompt": "How many factors does $1\\,048\\,576=2^{20}$ have?",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$21$",
          "worked": "The factors are $1,2,2^2,2^3,\\ldots,2^{20}$. These use none, one, two, and so on up to twenty factors of $2$. There are $21$ choices, including $1$, so there are $21$ factors.",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 24
      },
      {
        "id": "p31-q11-b",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "b",
        "prompt": "How many factors does $729=3^6$ have?",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$7$",
          "worked": "The factors are $1,3,3^2,3^3,3^4,3^5,3^6$, or $1,3,9,27,81,243,729$. There are $7$ factors.",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 24
      },
      {
        "id": "p31-q11-c",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "c",
        "prompt": "How many factors does $2^{20}\\times3^6$ have?",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$147$\n\nPair each of the $21$ possible powers of $2$ with each of the $7$ possible powers of $3$.",
          "worked": "A factor can contain none, one, two, and so on up to twenty factors of $2$: $21$ choices. It can also contain none, one, two, and so on up to six factors of $3$: $7$ choices.\n\nFor each choice of the power of $3$, there are $21$ choices of the power of $2$. Unique prime factorisation means these products are all different, and every factor is included.\n\n$$21\\times7=147$$\n\nThere are $147$ factors.",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 42
      }
    ]
